  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Agriculture obligated $129M on contracts in FY2027 to date. The Department of Agriculture recorded 1,452 awards with an average award size of $88.9K. Obligations fell 98.8% year over year, and current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress. Logging is the largest category so far at $99.6M, followed by Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation at $17M and Support Activities for Forestry at $16.6M. PEACHTREE LUMBER COMPANY, INC leads vendors with $99.6M in obligations, and other notable vendors include MICROSOFT CORPORATION at $7.6M and ASSOCIATED MILK PRODUCERS INC at $6.2M. The Department of Agriculture’s FY22 to FY26 annual obligations ranged from $9.6B to $11.6B, contrasting sharply with the FY27 to date total. This snapshot shows a concentrated set of high-dollar forestry and logistics contracts in the early part of FY2027 alongside a much smaller total obligation count for the partial year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How big is Agriculture's FY2027 contract program so far?",
        "body": "The Department of Agriculture obligated $129M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Agriculture issued 1,452 awards with an average award size of $88.9K. Obligations fell 98.8% year over year, and the current total is partial because the fiscal year is ongoing."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which industries and vendors are winning the most in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Logging is the largest industry category at $99.6M, followed by Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation at $17M and Support Activities for Forestry at $16.6M. PEACHTREE LUMBER COMPANY, INC is the top vendor at $99.6M, with MICROSOFT CORPORATION at $7.6M and ASSOCIATED MILK PRODUCERS INC at $6.2M. Several IT and services vendors appear on the top list, including KONIAG TECHNOLOGY SOLUTIONS INC at $5.2M and THUNDERCAT TECHNOLOGY, LLC at $4.9M."
      }
    ]
  },
