      "q": "How much does Department of Agriculture spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Agriculture obligated $129M on contracts in FY2027 to date. The Department of Agriculture recorded 1,452 awards with an average award size of $88.9K. Obligations fell 98.8% year over year, and the current total is partial because the fiscal year is ongoing."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Agriculture buy?",
      "a": "The Department of Agriculture buys a mix of forestry, air transport, food service, and IT services. Logging accounted for $99.6M, Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation accounted for $17M, Support Activities for Forestry accounted for $16.6M, and Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services accounted for $7.6M."
